<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them. In 2025 that pair hit 62% and August to September hit 61%. So far in 2026 on the middle, January to February sits at 51% and March to April at 205%. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 26581 down to 60%.</p>"}
